permitted only if all Covered Work functionality and included practice content
remain available without payment or a purchase requirement. You may not use the
Covered Work as an advertising-monetized service. Optional, unconditional
donations that give no additional access or preferential features are allowed.

4. Source sharing
When distributing the Covered Work or a modified version, provide recipients
with its complete corresponding source at no charge under this same license.
When publicly hosting the Covered Work or a modified version, prominently offer
every user a no-charge link to the complete corresponding source of the version
being hosted. Include the original and modified application source, question
data you are authorized to redistribute, and build and deployment instructions.
Do not include user records, secrets, credentials, or personal runtime databases.
Private modifications need not be published unless distributed or publicly hosted.

5. Same terms and notices
Covered modifications and derivatives must retain this license and its free
access, noncommercial, source-sharing, and attribution requirements. Preserve
copyright notices, this license text, applicable third-party notices, and
question-source attribution. Identify material modifications and do not imply
endorsement by this project's contributors or any question creator. You may not
impose additional terms that prevent recipients exercising the rights granted
here. Independent third-party components retain their own terms.

6. Preserving the collection
Redistributed or publicly hosted versions of the Covered Work must retain the
included baseline collected question entries, their source attribution, and any
authorized source artifacts. Duplicates may be linked and questions may be
corrected or marked unsuitable for scored exams, but their source records must
remain accessible. Additional questions are welcome. If retention would violate
an applicable law or a third party's rights or permission, remove the affected
material and document the reason without redistributing restricted material.

